# Firmware tuning, read by firmware.service when the firmware starts.
#
# Every value is commented out at its built-in default. To override one,
# uncomment it, change the value, then run `systemctl restart firmware`.
# A value that is not a whole number or is outside its range stops the
# firmware; `journalctl -u firmware` names the variable and its range.

## Hall-sensor scanning; see `docs/host.md#reading-the-board`.

# Target period of one complete eight-bank scan.
# Range: 5 to 1000 ms.
#FIRMWARE_HALL_SCAN_INTERVAL_MS=25

# Consecutive complete scans that must agree before a piece change is
# reported. The sensors themselves only sample every 27-75 ms.
# Range: 1 to 20 scans.
#FIRMWARE_HALL_STABLE_SCANS=2

## Control-panel buttons.

# How often each button line is sampled.
# Range: 1 to 100 ms.
#FIRMWARE_BUTTON_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=5

# How long a new level must hold before it counts as a press or release.
# Range: 1 to 500 ms.
#FIRMWARE_BUTTON_DEBOUNCE_MS=20
